{"id":"word:hebrew:H681","type":"word","title":"אֵצֶל","subtitle":"H681 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a side ; (as a preposition) near","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אֵצֶל (H681) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 61 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אֵצֶל (ʼêtsel) means a side ; (as a preposition) near First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 1 9."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אֵצֶל","transliteration":"ʼêtsel","pronunciation":"ay'-tsel","strong":"H681","lemmaId":"hebrew:H681","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["אֵ֣צֶל","אֵ֖צֶל","אֵ֥צֶל","אֵ֚צֶל","אֶצְלָ֑/ם"],"morphs":[["HR",39],["HR/Sp3ms",5],["HR/Sp1cs",4],["HR/Sp3fs",3],["HR/Sp3mp",3],["HR/R/Sp3ms",2],["HR/R",2],["HR/R/Sp1cs",1],["HR/R/Sp3mp",1],["HC/R",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a side ; (as a preposition) near","usage":"at, (hard) by, (from) (beside), near (unto), toward, with. See also 1018 .","full":"H681. etsel I. אֵ֫צֶל 61 substantive conjunction, proximity ; with suffix אֶצְלוֺ אֶצְלִי, etc.; only used as a preposition a. (as an implicit accusative) in proximity to (as though Lag BN 68 ), beside: Gen 39:10 , 15 ; 41:3 and stood הַמַּרוֺת אֵצֶל beside the kine, 1Sam 5:2 דָּגוֺן אֵצֶל beside Dagon, 1Kin 13:24-25 , 21:1 ; Prov 8:30 ; Ezek 1:15 , 19 ; 33:30 ; 39:15 ; often in phrase ( ׳מ ׳י ) הַמִּזְבֵּחַ אֵצֶל Lev 1:16 ; 6:3 ; Deut 16:21 ; 1Kin 2:29 ; Amos 2:8 +; of a locality (compare II. אֵת 2 ) Deut 11:30 beside the terebinths of Moreh, 1Kin 1:9 ; 4:12 ; Jer 41:17 . After a verb of motion (late) Dan 8:7 , 17 ; compare 2Chr 28:15 b. b. with מֵאֵצֶל מִן, from proximity to, from beside (compare מֵעִם מֵאֵת, ): 1Sam 20:41 (read with הָאַרְגָּב מֵאֵצֶל ᵐ5 from beside the mound); Ezek 40:7 contiguous to, beside ( מִן 3c ); with suffix 1Sam 17:30 מֵאֶצְלוֺ וַיָּסָב and he turned about from beside him , 1Kin 3:20 ; 20:36 ; Ezek 10:16 .","rootNote":"from 680